{include:`layouts/default.html.dtmpl`}
  {fill:content}
    {if:content.body}
      {comment}
        THE HERO IS INSIDE THE CONTENT BRANCH, and that is the fix for
        `<h1>Default</h1>`. The site label is a LABEL -- an internal name for a
        section, defaulting to the literal string "Default" -- and promoting it
        into the first line of text on a site is how a fresh installation
        introduced itself to a stranger. A site that has written a front page has
        also chosen its label, so there the heading is theirs; a site that has
        not gets the panel below instead of a heading nobody wrote.
      {endcomment}
      <section class="py-5 text-center bg-primary text-white rounded-3 mb-4">
        <div class="container">
          <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold">{var:site.label}</h1>
          {comment}
            GUARDED because an absent description printed an EMPTY <p class="lead">
            -- a gap the height of a line, which reads as something that failed to
            load rather than as something not yet written.
          {endcomment}
          {if:page.meta.description}
            <p class="lead">{var:page.meta.description}</p>
          {endif}
          {if:routes.login}
            <a href="{var:routes.login}" class="btn btn-light btn-lg mt-3">Get started</a>
          {endif}
        </div>
      </section>
      <div class="py-2">
        {var:content.body raw}
      </div>
    {else}
      {comment}
        THE FIRST-RUN BLOCK. It answers the only two questions a person has in
        the first two minutes -- did it work, and where do I go next -- and it is
        deliberately the page's CONTENT slot rather than a banner bolted on top:
        the moment anyone writes a front page, this disappears on its own.
        Nothing to find, nothing to switch off, no setting to discover.

        That is also why it is not styled like a designed page. A default that
        looks like a design decision is one a new user starts trying to remove
        instead of replace.
      {endcomment}
      <div class="py-5">
        <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm">
          <div class="card-body p-4 p-md-5">
            <p class="text-uppercase text-secondary small fw-semibold mb-2">Default page</p>
            <h1 class="h4 mb-3">Your installation is working.</h1>
            <p class="mb-4">
              This is the page CoolMS serves before anyone has written one. It is
              ordinary content — open it in the admin and replace it, and this text
              is gone.
            </p>
            <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
              <a href="/admin" class="btn btn-primary">Open the admin</a>
              <a href="https://github.com/coolms" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Source and packages</a>
            </div>
            <p class="text-secondary small mb-0">
              Signed in already? The front page lives under <strong>Content</strong>.
              Everything else on this page — the header, the footer — comes from the
              active theme.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    {endif}
  {endfill}
{endinclude}
